Pelagia @VERSION@ - unofficial Jellyfin client for PS5
Pelagia - client Jellyfin non officiel pour PS5
=====================================================

Not affiliated with the Jellyfin project or Sony. For hardware you own.
Non affilie au projet Jellyfin ni a Sony. Reserve a du materiel que vous possedez.
Project / Projet : @REPO_URL@


ENGLISH
-------
Tested with: PS5 firmware 13.60 (Relapse jailbreak), etaHEN, kstuff lite,
ftpsrv, websrv, ShadowMountPlus, Jellyfin server 12.1.0. HTTP only for now.

Install from a USB stick (easiest)
  1. Use a USB stick formatted as exFAT.
  2. Unzip this archive at the ROOT of the stick. You must get:
         <stick>/homebrew/Pelagia/eboot.elf
         <stick>/homebrew/Pelagia/sce_sys/icon0.png
     (INSTALL.txt may be deleted from the stick.)
  3. Plug the stick into the PS5, load your jailbreak setup so that websrv runs.
  4. Open the websrv launcher and start "Pelagia".
  Pelagia always stores its session, cache and logs in /data/homebrew/Pelagia/
  on the console, never on the stick.

Install over FTP (alternative)
  Copy the homebrew/Pelagia folder to /data/homebrew/Pelagia/ on the console
  (ftpsrv, port 2121), then start "Pelagia" from the websrv launcher.

First start
  Enter your Jellyfin server address (http://192.168.1.x:8096), your user name
  and your password with the on-screen keyboard. To skip typing the address,
  copy pelagia.conf.example to pelagia.conf (same folder) and edit "server=".
  It is read from the stick first, then from /data/homebrew/Pelagia/.

Controller: D-pad/left stick = move, Cross = select, Circle = back,
  Triangle = play/pause, L1/R1 = -/+10 s, L2/R2 = -/+60 s, Options = menu.

If something goes wrong
  Logs are in /data/homebrew/Pelagia/logs/pelagia.log (read them over FTP).
  The token and the password never appear in the logs.
  Known limit: after "Quit", the screen may stay black; close the websrv
  launcher by hand.

